# Config form notes
config-tls-forced = TLS is always on for this protocol (security locked tls).
config-mux-vision = Mux is unavailable with the xtls-rprx-vision flow — stored mux keys are preserved.
config-brutal-mux = Brutal requires mux (forced On).
config-ss-plugin-note = Plugin rows need the plugin executable beside the engine — stock check fails without it.
config-wg-note = WireGuard rows become endpoints[] at generate. Blank AllowedIPs defaults to 0.0.0.0/0; DNS is stored but never emitted; udp_timeout stays JSON-only.
config-awg-note = AmneziaWG rows run in the fork sidecar (sing-box-awg). v3-only keys on a 2.0 row fail generate naming the field; udp_timeout stays JSON-only.
config-awg-v3-hidden = v3-only fields hidden — stored values preserved (never wiped).
config-hy-note = Hysteria v1 rows require up/down (blank refuses naming up_mbps/down_mbps); v2 omits them for BBR. v1-only keys on a v2 row fail generate naming the field.
config-tuic-note = TUIC runs TLS always-on (security locked tls). Blank congestion/relay stay unset.
config-socks-note = SOCKS serves version 5 stock (blank leaves the default); 4 fails generate naming version. Blank network leaves tcp.
config-http-note = HTTPS rows serve TLS-on (security=tls) even with the panel off. Path/headers ride the http outbound — check judges the headers shape.
config-anytls-note = AnyTLS runs TLS always-on (security locked tls). Interval/timeout are durations (e.g. 30s); min is a session count.
config-naive-note = Naïve runs TLS always-on (security locked tls). Blank congestion control leaves the default (cubic).
config-ssh-note = Browse fills the path and loads the key file (no hand-paste). Host key lists are comma-separated; cipher/mac/kex stay JSON-only.
config-snell-note = Snell serves version 4 when blank; 6 needs a v6 peer. Obfs/userkey/reuse/network/mode ride the snell outbound — check judges their shapes.
config-shadowtls-note = ShadowTLS runs TLS always-on (security locked tls). Version blank takes the schema default 1; v1 rows omit the password.
config-xray-note = Ph1 subset only — XHTTP/xmux/session keys (xPaddingBytes, maxConcurrency, downloadSettings…) stay JSON-only and are preserved, never stripped.
config-chain-note = V1 chains are flat: no chain hops; at most one extra-core hop, first only. Extra/Custom/Xray hops must be last — the engine names violations at start.
config-extra-note = Spawned unprivileged as <exe> -c <config-file> (v1 convention — extra flags ride args with the row). Validate checks exe + config shape before commit; there is no logs toggle by design.
lan-hint = Leaving loopback exposes this machine — starting on { $bind } needs a LAN confirm, and anyone on the network could use it
